A||N||8||NOS3800||Failed attempt at Fastest V6||||8||
Z||000000||NOS3800||10-06-2001||12:29 AM||||Tonite I tried to steal away 1FST2M6's position as the fastest V6. Upon conversing with him via email, we determined that I should lean out my system cause it was running rich. I was wary but decided to take his advice. MAN what a difference! <BR>First run went from 38 NOS jet to a 43 NOS jet. Ran a 13.21 at 101.44. Had a little slip and chirp from the tires, had 1.856 60'.<BR>Since this run went sooo well, it truly felt GREAT!, I went to a 46 jet.<BR>This is where things got scary. First run, spun all the way through first, got off it and back in. It spun again! I still ran a13.472 at 101.70, 60' was 2.061. <BR>Next run I did a little burn out. I launched without spraying till the car was in motion. My 60' was 1.976. I think I waited too long to spray. I ran a 13.335 at 102.13! All these times are new fastest for me. It turns out my bottle was 5 pounds low. I went to get my bottle topped off for my trip to NJ for the HPP shootout, just incase they ask me to run, and the attendent said my bottle only had 5 pounds in it. 3 runs equals 5 pounds of NOS? Thats pretty extreme. i need to stop purging me thinks.<BR>So you can sleep soundly for one more week 1FST2M6, next weekend I will get things right, hopefully anyway!||||reg||8
Z||000001||Leper||10-06-2001||01:45 AM||||Here's a consolation prize.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NOS3800.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||10-06-2001||10:42 AM||||Hey I will give you lots of credit for trying to get into the 12's.  At least you are trying it instead of just talking about trying to do it.<P>you are close to 12's  just a little bit more.  Yess don't purge so much.  its very wastefull.  You only need to do it right before you launch and only barely push the button.  You don't need to hold it.  Just push it for a quick tenth of a second and if there is any air/non liquid it will be expelled in that time since the bottle is under extreme pressure as you know already.  Purge it when you are staged and the other car is staged right before the yellows start to go.  <P>I never purged my nitrous but thats because I didnt' buy a kit for it.  I saw it as wasting nitrous and at $3 a pound it could get expensive.  I always had my bottle closed at the track when not running it so I really didn't see a need to purge.  Plus I was told that pending on how much nitrous you run a purge will only get you about .1 gain in the qtr.  I figured low 14's was good enough without spending another $100 on a purge. <P>What you should do it get some skinny's up front or raise your tire pressure in the front to 10-15 over the recommened maximum.  Like if the max recommended is 35 then put 45-50 psi in it.  This will lower rolling resistance.  Also try and take some stuff out of the car like the passenger seat and the spare tire and jack if you still have them in there.  Both these combined are 60 pounds which could take off about .1 or so.  Could try icing down your intake and throttle body while in the pre-staging lanes.  Just put a big bag of ice on it.  I am sure you know why.  Don't know if you have done this or not but I thought I would suggest it just in case.<P>Is your torque converter locking up when you go down the track?  In my Fiero my 125c would lock up the converter after 3rd gear kicked in.  So what I did was unplugged my TCC lockup switch from the side of the tranny and picked up a tenth or two from that.  I dont' know if it does with your tranny since it is different but if there is a way to disconnect it from locking up then try that.  <P>They make underdrive pulleys for the n/a 3800?  If they do and you dont' have that yet then that would also help get you into the 12's.  I picked about .1 after I put on an underdrive pulley on my 2.8.<P>Watch that nitrous so you don't add too much and keep an eye on those sparkplugs!!  Cant' stress that enough.  They are a good indicator of whats happening in the combustion chamber.  I would hate for you to  run lean and bust a piston just to try and get a 12.9.  I would rather see you run numerous 13.0's and safely if that is all your engine is willing to do.<P>Congrats on your low 13 man.  Thats  moving really good and your car is hooking up well too.  I hope you make 12's in the future.  if you do any racing on the street I am sure you surprise a lot of people.  I know I did and I was a whole second slower then you.  Hehe  Keep us all updated<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||14
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||10-06-2001||12:32 PM||||Sounds like you have been having fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Just be careful, don't want to get tooo lean on fuel.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000004||NOS3800||10-06-2001||02:02 PM||||First off, thanks LEPER, I needed to resize my sig pic anyway. Can I use that pic as my sig?<BR>Shaun, I purge where you say to, right when the we both get the first staging lights lit. BUT, I do push the button way too long. Its addicting, and judging from the reactions from the video I have, the fans like it. But money speaks, I will not purge anymore unless the guy next to me does <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">! Since adding the purge, it did knock a tenth off, and relly made a difference off the line. 60's went from high 1.900 to high 1.800. <BR>I checked my plugs today, and they are silver to grey, which makes me believe it was lean. I am bumping the jet back to 43 until I can find a jet that will bump up my fuel. Jegs and Summit sells jets, but they only work on NOS kits, not ZEX. Anyone know where I can get jets for non-NOS kits? I spoke to a rep at ZEX and he says NOS kits use a unique jet, where as every other kit uses a universal design.<BR>About the TCC, I am not sure if it is locking up in third or not, but I don't think there is a way to disconnect this on a 4T60E tranny, everything is computer controlled but I will ask a friend who works on transmissions.<BR>I do not have underdrive pulleys, but I have removed the powersteering pump and pulley, so I am sure that is just as good. <BR>I will try the tire pressure thing, and will be getting fatter tires in the rear. I have (don't laugh) 215's in the rear now. I got them cheap, Dunlop W-10's and couldn't pass on them.<BR>I have the spare tire and jack removed. I don't like removing the seats cause I like to run close to street trim as possible. I see all these yahoos with their Civics completely stripped. They have HUGE piles of seats, carpets, wheels and a kitchen sink where their car parks in the pits <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">. They go out and run a low 16 maybe high 15. I just look and wonder why go through the trouble?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shaun41178||10-06-2001||02:31 PM||||if purging helps then go for it.  Just dont' hold down on it.  just tap the button real quick and it will clear the line and save you lots of juice too.  Don't worry what the crowd thinks.  They will be impressed after your run more then at the beginning of it when your E.T flashes.<P>If you are hooking good off the line then no need to get wider tires.  I used 215 60 14 on my car as well so no I am not laughing.  At one time I even think I had 195-14's on it and I still hooked great.  I was still able to cut 1.8 60's but mostly got 1.9's  It doesnt' seem like you spin that bad out of the hole so stay with that size or go to 225 or something.  don't go too wide or you will counteract the effects of raising front tire pressure.  Also if you do spin a bit bring tire pressure down a bit in the rear.  In my tires I found I hooked best and ran the fastest with 28 psi in the rears.  Lower pressure in the rears 1-2 psi at a time and see if you hook better without the need to go to wider tires.<P>Good idea about teh powersteering pump since you don't need it anyways.  By also adding a  underdrive crank and perhaps alternator pulley you can slow down the alternator and water pump thus giving you even a few more hp.  Depends on how far you want to go I guess.<P>I never changed the jetting on my car.  when I first started going to the track I was running 14.8-9's.  By doing little tricks like the pulley and playing with tire pressure and iceing intake and the TCC I was able to get it down to a 14.2.  On the same jetting remember.  So .6 is pretty good.  You probably won't see the same gains like me but its little things like that, that help lower the e.t without adding more nitrous and run the risk of engine failure.<P>Which reminds me of a story when I was at the strip one time.<P>I was in the staging lines hanging with my car and some people come up and start talking and all this.  Not super nice things.  Then they see the bottle and are like wow cool.  They had a video camera there with them filming the cars and stuff.  So I was telling them what it runs and all this stuff.  It is now my turn to race so I go around the box and these guys with the camcorders are right there next to me going to film me leave the line and stuff.  So I am going up there and my car starts to sputter and run like crap.  I was like WTF.  Then it stalls out.  I was like uh oh I think I burned up my ignition module.  Try to start it and sure enough no spark as the tach is dead.  So the guys with the camera just looked at me wierd as I pushed my car out of the way.  How embarassing is that!! I was telling these guys that it is a pretty quick car and this and that and when I get up there is doesn't want to stay running.  STUPID POS FIERO!! HAHAHA!.  I replaced my ignition module as I always keep a spare with me and jump back in the staging lanes again.  But when I do the guys are gone probably looking at other cars or something.  oh well.  funny now but kind of sucked back then at the time.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Leper||10-06-2001||07:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NOS3800:<BR><B>First off, thanks LEPER, I needed to resize my sig pic anyway. Can I use that pic as my sig?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Go right ahead, that's why I made it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||BBBAD GT||10-07-2001||08:53 AM||||Here's an idea (take it how you want), but instead of purging all the time, just don't purge and hit the button sooner, like just off idle.  Because the 'hit' won't be so great, you won't spin as much off idle and maybe you'll have enough momentum to keep it from spinning when the good stuff hits (this is how guys with N2O kits say they hit it right off idle).  Its sort of like a progressive hit.  Nothing breaks parts or disrupts a run more than having a huge 'hit'.  A progressive controller or a multi stage kit (in my opinion) will always be better in the long run.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||NOS3800||10-07-2001||11:40 PM||||Thanks for the advice BBADGT. I think I am going to use it too, after what you and Shaun have said. I also kinda realized your points on my ride home from the track. I will not purge anymore. The reason I got it was that there was a great deal of lag when using the 38 jet. I think this may have been a result of being really rich on top of whatever vapor was in the line. It did improve my 60's with the 38 jet. Once I upped to the 43 and 46, tranny failure is a concern if I hookup! It is soo strong it is scary, and when the car gets loose, it likes to fishtail! Which is fun to watch, but not much fun to drive! I will keep everyone posted. this weekend will be round two!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||12
